00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:08.280
That's some of the reason that some people&nbsp;
will get fussy about sleeping together. A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:17.340
lot of it is about movement. Also snoring is&nbsp;
a big concern with desiring a sleep divorce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:20.760
or it's a motivating factor, I should say.
Tim Ferriss: So we've talked about one direction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:28.200
We've talked about how sleep affects sex. What&nbsp;
about the other direction? Is sex helpful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:34.200
deleterious to sleep quality? What&nbsp;
are the factors if someone's trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:40.600
to give themselves the optimal dose of sex&nbsp;
to improve sleep, if there is such a thing?&nbsp;

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:44.760
Dr. Matthew Walker: Yeah. And one should never&nbsp;
