00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:17.460
and you have to work with someone who's going&nbsp;
to motivate you, and it is hard, but it works.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:18.120 --> 00:41:24.240
And after the second night of being in bed for&nbsp;
five hours, you've been awake for longer. So now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:24.240 --> 00:41:29.400
you've been awake for 19 hours during the day&nbsp;
and you're only in bed assuming for five hours.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:30.300 --> 00:41:35.580
And that increase in your adenosine&nbsp;
because you're awake now for 19 hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:35.580 --> 00:41:40.440
straight for one day, for a second day, for&nbsp;
a third day, it all starts to accumulate.&nbsp;

00:41:41.040 --> 00:41:45.720
And then at one point, maybe, and it depends on&nbsp;
the patient, let's say about four or five days&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:45.720 --> 00:41:52.680
after that, they get into bed at 2:30 a.m. or 3:00&nbsp;
